    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0403" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg297"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister
                    Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 157.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a copy of a dispatch
                    from the consul-general at Shanghai, inclosing a copy of a letter to be
                    addressed by the senior consul of the consular body at Shanghai to the dean of
                    the diplomatic corps at Peking, protesting against the restrictions threatened
                    by the Chinese on the natural growth of the foreign settlement at Shanghai
                    toward the north and east. I also inclose a copy of the department’s answer,
                    approving the proposed letter.</p>
                <p>You will support the request of the consular body unless you see some serious
                    objection.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>




